// LIFE DIRECTOR CONTRACT v1 (DIRECTOR01)
type DirectorSlot='P2'|'P3'|'P4'|'P5'|'P6'|'CONTINUATION';
type DirectorHints={salience:1|2|3|4|5;baseWeight?:number;topicTags:string[];continuityTags:string[];buildAffinityTags:string[];npcRoleAffinityTags:string[];worldAffinityTags:string[];onboardingEligible?:boolean};
type DirectorSceneRecord={eventId:string;nodeIndex:number;slot:DirectorSlot;salience:1|2|3|4|5;topicTags:string[];continuityTags:string[];actorIds:string[];buildIds:string[];causeId?:string;riskTier?:'low'|'caution'|'dangerous'|'lethal'};
type DirectorState={profileId:'standard'|'first_run'|string;recentScenes:DirectorSceneRecord[]};

Selector precedence is strict: P1 terminal/lifespan; P2 first-run Director; P3 eligible Cause echo; P4 met+active core NPC; P5 action/Build/world/generated-NPC context; P6 ordinary fallback.
The first level with eligible candidates wins. Unimplemented systems provide zero candidates. Authored continuation stays CONTINUATION and is not reselected.
P2 is available only for profileId first_run, onboardingEligible content, and nodeIndex<=3. It may guide but cannot force complete system coverage.
P3 remains Cause-owned: Cause priority/budget/linked-event selection is unchanged and random pacing must not suppress a valid echo.
P4 requires an indexed role binding to a met, active core NPC. P5 uses indexed actionAffinity/build/world/met-active-generated-NPC signals. Unknown NPC state is never inferred.
P4 additionally excludes a candidate whose matched core actor ids intersect the core actor ids of the single most recent DirectorSceneRecord ('core-npc-repeat-gate'). The gate reads DirectorSceneRecord.actorIds verbatim and nothing else: no content lookup, no role re-derivation. It consults only that one record, so one intervening scene with no matching core actor clears it; it changes candidate eligibility only and never precedence, scoring, or ordering. Actor provenance on records is exact: every recorded scene stores the actors it was actually bound to, and for a P3 Cause echo the reducer persists the exact selected CauseInstance.actorIdsByRole (the causeId already persisted as events.current.triggeringCauseId), never a templateId/role/salience/uniqueness lookup or a re-derivation from Event tags. A P3 echo therefore blocks an immediate same-core-NPC P4 rebound using the echo's authoritative actors, which stays correct when several active core NPC instances share one role.
P5 additionally excludes a candidate while any of the last contextualGapScenes DirectorSceneRecords is itself a P5 scene ('contextual-gap'). The gate counts DirectorSceneRecords, not node distance, so two later non-P5 scenes reopen P5 on their own. It exists because the P5 contextual tier is otherwise populated at essentially every action node, which would permanently shadow the P6 ordinary fallback and make it unreachable. It reads only the existing bounded recentScenes ring and changes P5 candidate eligibility only: it adds no state, counter, timer, or RNG draw, and leaves precedence, P4 eligibility, P6 eligibility, scoring, and ordering untouched. v1 value: contextualGapScenes = 2.

Director metadata is versioned Content: stable IDs, declared tags, safe-integer values, no executable hooks/scripts/functions.
Default/baseWeight range is 100 / 1..1000. Score deltas: action +80; Build emerging +25, formed +50, refined +75; world +40; recent NPC +50; continuity +30 each capped +60; novel topic +20; recent exact event -80; consecutive topic -30 each capped -60.
Scoring and candidate order are canonical and insertion-order independent. Content IDs are not hardcoded in Core.
At a selected priority: 0 candidates => next priority/no RNG; 1 => direct/no RNG; 2+ => eventId ASC canonical input then one logical unbiased weighted request on the director stream. Rejection sampling may consume multiple underlying draws and all are traced.

Random P5/P6 major scenes (salience>=4) require a 2-node gap. Random dangerous/lethal scenes require a 1-node gap. Authored Cause/continuation flow is exempt.
DirectorState stores only a bounded recent ring (v1 size 8) of compact references/tags; never full event bodies, dialogue, candidate lists, weights, or hidden future plans.
Trace records selected precedence/slot/event, candidate and eligible counts, selected weight, exclusion reason counts, director draw indexes, continuity reasons, logical request count, and index-query stats.
Director may choose eligible content only. It cannot mutate stats/resources/Build/NPC/Cause, decide Check/Outcome/death/rewards, roll outcome RNG, or call AI/platform/network/time services.
ContentRegistry must maintain eventId and Director tag indexes. Hot-path selection must not scan the full Event library or all NPC instances.
Short lives may omit systems; long lives use pacing rather than quotas. New Event/Build/NPC/World content extends through Definitions/Tags/Registry without Core algorithms changing.
